[{"category":"section","location":"theory/gauge_transform/#Gauge-Transformation-and-Unitary-Equivalence","page":"Gauge Transformation","text":"The transformation between the real symmetric operator A_0 and the phase-dependent operator A_omegatau is a unitary similarity transformation (gauge transformation).","title":"Gauge Transformation & Unitary Equivalence"},{"category":"section","location":"theory/gauge_transform/#1.-Operator-Formulations","page":"Gauge Transformation","text":"Let A_0 be the real quadrature operator with tau = 0:\n\nA_0 = frac1sqrt2omega left( a + a^dagger right)\n\nIn the truncated Fock basis nrangle_n=0^N-1, A_0 has matrix elements:\n\nlangle m  A_0  n rangle = frac1sqrt2omega left( sqrtndelta_m n-1 + sqrtn+1delta_m n+1 right)\n\nThis corresponds to a SymTridiagonal matrix with zero diagonal and e_n = sqrtn  sqrt2omega.\n\nThe phase-dependent operator is:\n\nA_omegatau = frac1sqrt2omega left( e^-iomegatau a + e^iomegatau a^dagger right)","title":"1. Operator Formulations"},{"category":"section","location":"theory/gauge_transform/#2.-Unitary-Phase-Matrix","page":"Gauge Transformation","text":"Define the diagonal phase rotation matrix U:\n\nU = operatornamediagleft(1 e^-iomegatau e^-2iomegatau dots e^-i(N-1)omegatauright)\n\nwhere U_mn = e^-inomegataudelta_mn.","title":"2. Unitary Phase Matrix"},{"category":"section","location":"theory/gauge_transform/#3.-Proof-of-Similarity-(A_{\\omega\\tau}-U-A_0-U\\dagger)","page":"Gauge Transformation","text":"beginaligned\n(U A_0 U^dagger)_mn = sum_jk U_mj (A_0)_jk (U^dagger)_kn \n= e^-i(m-n)omegatau (A_0)_mn\nendaligned\n\nEvaluating non-zero entries:\n\nSuperdiagonal (m = n - 1): (U A_0 U^dagger)_n-1n = e^iomegatau (A_0)_n-1n\nSubdiagonal (m = n + 1): (U A_0 U^dagger)_n+1n = e^-iomegatau (A_0)_n+1n\n\nThus, A_omegatau = U A_0 U^dagger exactly.","title":"3. Proof of Similarity (A_omegatau = U A_0 U^dagger)"},{"category":"section","location":"theory/gauge_transform/#4.-Eigenvalue-and-Eigenvector-Mapping","page":"Gauge Transformation","text":"For A_0 mathbfv_textreal = lambda mathbfv_textreal, substituting A_0 = U^dagger A_omegatau U yields:\n\nA_omegatau (U mathbfv_textreal) = lambda (U mathbfv_textreal)\n\nEigenvalues: Unchanged (lambda).\nEigenvectors: mathbfv_textcomplex = U mathbfv_textreal.\n\nIn Julia, multiplying row n of V_textreal by e^-inomegatau executes U mathbfv_textreal exactly.\n\n","title":"4. Eigenvalue & Eigenvector Mapping"},{"category":"section","location":"theory/gauge_transform/#API-Reference","page":"Gauge Transformation","text":"","title":"API Reference"},{"category":"section","location":"#nonKam.jl-Documentation","page":"Home","text":"Welcome to the documentation for nonKam.jl.","title":"nonKam.jl Documentation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Overview","page":"Home","text":"Gauge Transformation Theory","title":"Overview"}]
